Local review patch: validate the complete T6032 CPU inventory before startup
Base: m1n1 4184923ffb2dff079b384d6a32cc02142aa14572, after 0001..0005
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Preflight all 32 CPU nodes before the boot CPU RVBAR path or any secondary
release. Reject duplicate IDs/coordinates, inconsistent affinity, ambiguous
boot state and invalid/overlapping implementation-register windows. Require
explicit cpu-impl-reg; do not use the legacy arm-io/reg fallback on T6032.
Read properties with validated lengths before decoding, not ADT_GETPROP.

This does not enable T6032 dispatch, validate MPIDR/entry state or establish
RVBAR writability. It adds no hardware access. Other SoCs bypass the check.
The existing void startup/caller API and whole-boot behavior are unchanged.

--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
